ata-end="887"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_15" data-source="" data-orig="Quinoa">Quinoa</span> (<em data-start="746" data-end="766"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_16" data-source="" data-orig="Chenopodium quinoa">Chenopodium quinoa</span></em>) <span class ="tr_" id="tr_17" data-source="" data-orig="is often called a “pseudo-cereal” because it’s not a true grain but is used similarly">is often called a “pseudo-cereal” because it’s not a true grain but is used similarly</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_18" data-source="" data-orig="Here are the key specifications">Here are the key specifications</span>:</p><ul data-start="889" data-end="2036"><li data-start="889" data-end="1095"><p data-start="891" data-end="912"><strong data-start="891" data-end="912">Источник &amp; История:</strong></p><ul data-start="915" data-end="1095"><li data-start="915" data-end="988"><strong data-start="917" data-end="935"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_19" data-source="" data-orig="Native Region">Native Region</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_20" data-source="" data-orig="South America">South America</span> (<span class ="tr_" id="tr_21" data-source="" data-orig="Andes region">Andes region</span>: <span class ="tr_" id="tr_22" data-source="" data-orig="Peru">Peru</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_23" data-source="" data-orig="Bolivia">Bolivia</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_24" data-source="" data-orig="Ecuador">Ecuador</span>)</li><li data-start="991" data-end="1095"><strong data-start="993" data-end="1021"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_25" data-source="" data-orig="Historical Significance">Historical Significance</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_26" data-source="" data-orig="Revered by the Incas as the “mother grain” and used in ceremonial dishes">Revered by the Incas as the “mother grain” and used in ceremonial dishes</span>.</li></ul></li><li data-start="1097" data-end="1353"><p data-start="1099" data-end="1113"><strong data-start="1099" data-end="1113">Разновидности:</strong></p><ul data-start="1116" data-end="1353"><li data-start="1116" data-end="1174"><strong data-start="1118" data-end="1135"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_27" data-source="" data-orig="White Quinoa">White Quinoa</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_28" data-source="" data-orig="Most common">Most common</span>; <span class ="tr_" id="tr_29" data-source="" data-orig="tender and mild-flavored">tender and mild-flavored</span>.</li><li data-start="1177" data-end="1260"><strong data-start="1179" data-end="1194"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_30" data-source="" data-orig="Red Quinoa">Red Quinoa</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_31" data-source="" data-orig="Has a slightly chewier texture">Has a slightly chewier texture</span>; <span class ="tr_" id="tr_32" data-source="" data-orig="ideal for salads and cold dishes">ideal for salads and cold dishes</span>.</li><li data-start="1263" data-end="1353"><strong data-start="1265" data-end="1282"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_33" data-source="" data-orig="Black Quinoa">Black Quinoa</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_34" data-source="" data-orig="Darker color with a stronger">Darker color with a stronger</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_35" data-source="" data-orig="earthier taste">earthier taste</span>; <span class ="tr_" id="tr_36" data-source="" data-orig="requires longer cooking">requires longer cooking</span>.</li></ul></li><li data-start="1355" data-end="1618"><p data-start="1357" data-end="1388"><strong data-start="1357" data-end="1388"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_37" data-source="" data-orig="Growing Conditions">Growing Conditions</span> &amp; Урожай:</strong></p><ul data-start="1391" data-end="1618"><li data-start="1391" data-end="1457"><strong data-start="1393" data-end="1405"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_38" data-source="" data-orig="Climate">Climate</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_39" data-source="" data-orig="Thrives in high-altitude">Thrives in high-altitude</span>, прохладный, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_40" data-source="" data-orig="and dry conditions">and dry conditions</span>.</li><li data-start="1460" data-end="1518"><strong data-start="1462" data-end="1471"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_41" data-source="" data-orig="Soil">Soil</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_42" data-source="" data-orig="Adapts well to poor soils with minimal inputs">Adapts well to poor soils with minimal inputs</span>.</li><li data-start="1521" data-end="1618"><strong data-start="1523" data-end="1533">Урожай:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_43" data-source="" data-orig="Approximately 1–2 tons per hectare">Approximately 1–2 tons per hectare</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_44" data-source="" data-orig="although yields vary with cultivation practices">although yields vary with cultivation practices</span>.</li></ul></li><li data-start="1620" data-end="1912"><p data-start="1622" data-end="1649"><strong data-start="1622" data-end="1649">Использование &amp; <span class ="tr_" id="tr_45" data-source="" data-orig="Cooking Methods">Cooking Methods</span>:</strong></p><ul data-start="1652" data-end="1912"><li data-start="1652" data-end="1733"><strong data-start="1654" data-end="1666"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_46" data-source="" data-orig="Rinsing">Rinsing</span>:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_47" data-source="" data-orig="Must be rinsed thoroughly to remove natural saponins">Must be rinsed thoroughly to remove natural saponins</span> (<span class ="tr_" id="tr_48" data-source="" data-orig="bitterness">bitterness</span>).</li><li data-start="1736" data-end="1810"><strong data-start="1738" data-end="1750">Кулинария:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_49" data-source="" data-orig="Use a water-to-quinoa ratio of">Use a water-to-quinoa ratio of</span> 2:1; <span class ="tr_" id="tr_50" data-source="" data-orig="boil for 15–20 minutes">boil for 15–20 minutes</span>.</li><li data-start="1813" data-end="1912"><strong data-start="1815" data-end="1832">Приложения:</strong> <span class ="tr_" id="tr_51" data-source="" data-orig="Ideal in salads">Ideal in salads</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_52" data-source="" data-orig="as a rice substitute">as a rice substitute</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_53" data-source="" data-orig="in porridges">in porridges</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_54" data-source="" data-orig="or even baked into snacks">or even baked into snacks</span>.</li></ul></li><li data-start="1914" data-end="2036"><p data-start="1916" data-end="1936"><strong data-start="1916" data-end="1936"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_55" data-source="" data-orig="Popular Regions">Popular Regions</span>:</strong></p><ul data-start="1939" data-end="2036"><li data-start="1939" data-end="2036"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_56" data-source="" data-orig="Gaining popularity in North America">Gaining popularity in North America</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_57" data-source="" data-orig="Europe">Europe</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_58" data-source="" data-orig="and parts of Asia due to its nutritional benefits">and parts of Asia due to its nutritional benefits</span>.</li></ul></li></ul><hr data-start="2038" data-end="2041" /><h2 data-start="2043" data-end="2065"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="2_What_Is_Korralu"></span>2. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_59" data-source="" data-orig="What Is Korralu">What Is Korralu</span>?<span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p data-start="2067" data-end="2236"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_60" data-source="" data-orig="Korralu is a term used in some regions to describe a type of millet or small grain">Korralu is a term used in some regions to describe a type of millet or small grain</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_61" data-source="" data-orig="Although less globally recognized than quinoa">Although less globally recognized than quinoa</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_62" data-source="" data-orig="it has its own set of unique features">it has its own set of unique features</span>:</p><ul data-start="2238" data-end="3386"><li data-sta